WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:06.610
I am sitting in the control room of the GSI
Institute, the

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:10.230
control room of the linear accelerator that
was used to create

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:16.870
element 111 and five of the other super-heavy
elements. The

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:23.650
idea of this is that you have a metal target,
usually lead or

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:31.480
bismuth, elements 82 or 83. And you take a
lighter element,

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:37.770
say copper and bang the copper at huge velocity
into the lead

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.850
or the bismuth, depending the element that
you want to

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:47.120
make. The idea is that you have to accelerate
them very fast

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.080
so that the two positively charged nuclei
can come together.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.970
But not so fast that you have a lot of energy
and they

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.100
immediately fall apart again.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.220
Ok, this is the periodic table of the elements
that was used

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:05.300
for the christening of element 111 which was
called

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.680
roentgenium. And you see you can remove this
cube here and

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:15.280
Sigurd Hofmann the head of the group who discovered
the

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.640
elements and our minister Annette Schavan
together inserted

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:24.170
the cube into the periodic table of the elements
and it actually

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:26.470
started to glow.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:33.830
Oh it was an amazing day, we had a huge ceremony,
1000

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:36.620
people came here for the christening and afterwards
there

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:40.140
was cake and champagne and it was really good.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:46.130
Element 111 has a name which is really difficult
to pronounce

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:50.190
- roentgenium which is named after Rontgen
the discoverer

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:55.130
of x-rays. I just find that it is a combination
of letters that

00:01:55.130 --> 00:02:00.200
people in England find difficult to pronounce.
However

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.220
Rontgen was, I believe, the first Nobel Prize
winner or one of

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:08.869
the first Nobel Prize winners and so it is
really quite fitting

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:13.840
that he should have an element named after
him.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:21.209
The first discovery was of three atoms, of
this element and

00:02:21.209 --> 00:02:24.230
then the experiments were repeated, and another
three were

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:29.760
found, so it was relatively still relatively
quite a small number,

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.959
but it is really important when somebody does
a series of

00:02:32.959 --> 00:02:36.959
these experiments that you have to repeat
them to make

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:40.849
sure that you have really seen what you think
you want. You

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:45.189
are really excited you want to make a new
element and so it

00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:49.669
is quite easy to fool yourself. Or sometimes
people could be

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:54.669
tempted to cheat so you really have to repeat
it. Ideally you

00:02:54.669 --> 00:02:57.989
get a different lab in a different place using
a different route

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:02.480
and if two people get the same results you
are pretty sure.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:07.599
But in this case I think the two runs were
repeated here and

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:12.569
it was still a whole period of 10 or 12 years
between the

00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:16.650
discovery of the element and it being finally
named. Because

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:23.250
people want to be absolutely sure that the
data are correct.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:28.340
The machines that makes these ions is enormous
and it takes

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:32.870
a whole team of operators to control it. And
all this stuff

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:38.560
behind me is to control the power, the voltages
and so on,

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.969
and the different parts of the accelerator
that takes the ion

00:03:42.969 --> 00:03:46.739
beam to this tiny chamber. It is really only
about this size,

00:03:46.739 --> 00:03:50.159
where the actual experiment took place and
once the atom is

00:03:50.159 --> 00:03:55.019
made it then flies off to the detector that
is two rooms away

00:03:55.019 --> 00:03:56.499
down a long tube.

00:03:56.499 --> 00:03:59.290
Yeah, of course we are waiting now for the
final confirmation

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:04.530
to christen element 112 which is going to
be copernicium, but

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:07.309
well we don’t know yet what we are going
to do for the

00:04:07.309 --> 00:04:10.010
christening. We are having discussions what
we are going to

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:12.119
do and I think it will be a big surprise.

